{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141Ar7oiMRFtmZWNA3FZV7E","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Mistral API DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} documentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MistralClient.API.Models — mistralex_ai v0.1.0\",\"url\":\"https://hexdocs.pm/mistralex_ai/MistralClient.API.Models.html\"},{\"title\":\"client-python/docs/sdks/models/README.md at main · mistralai/client-python\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mistralai/client-python/blob/main/docs/sdks/models/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Mistral AI API | Mistral AI\",\"url\":\"https://platform-docs-public.pages.dev/api/\"},{\"title\":\"openapi: 3.1.0 info: title: Mistral AI API description: >-\",\"url\":\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wso2/apk/refs/heads/main/samples/llm-providers-oas-definitions/mistral/mistral_api.yaml\"},{\"title\":\"Model Management | mistralai/client-python | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/mistralai/client-python/3.4-structured-output\"},{\"title\":\"docs.mistral.ai\",\"url\":\"https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/models\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's the information about the Mistral API DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} endpoint:\n\n## DELETE /v1/models/{model_id}\n\nThis endpoint deletes a fine-tuned model.\n\n### Parameters\nThe model_id is a required path parameter (string) that specifies the ID of the model to delete, with an example format like: ft:open-mistral-7b:587a6b29:20240514:7e773925.\n\n### Authentication\nThe endpoint requires ApiKey authentication.\n\n### Response\nThe endpoint returns a 200 status code for a successful response or 422 for validation errors. The response content type is application/json and includes an object with the model id and a \"deleted\": true field.\n\n### Important Restrictions\nYou can only delete fine-tuned models that you own. Base models cannot be deleted.\n\nYou can find the full API documentation at the official Mistral AI documentation site at https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/models.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc070dc6-ba02-43c5-a6da-e4c2a8dbe708","uuid":"754dc7f6-f4c8-490e-8b67-76cee624fd2b","timestamp":"2026-09-11T19:51:40.835Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Mistral API DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} documentation","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QtxTxf7QQupzswb9Z2j3w9","content":[{"title":"MistralClient.API.Models — mistralex_ai v0.1.0","url":"https://hexdocs.pm/mistralex_ai/MistralClient.API.Models.html"},{"title":"client-python/docs/sdks/models/README.md at main · mistralai/client-python","url":"https://github.com/mistralai/client-python/blob/main/docs/sdks/models/README.md"},{"title":"Mistral AI API | Mistral AI","url":"https://platform-docs-public.pages.dev/api/"},{"title":"openapi: 3.1.0 info: title: Mistral AI API description: >-","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wso2/apk/refs/heads/main/samples/llm-providers-oas-definitions/mistral/mistral_api.yaml"},{"title":"Model Management | mistralai/client-python | DeepWiki","url":"https://deepwiki.com/mistralai/client-python/3.4-structured-output"},{"title":"docs.mistral.ai","url":"https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/models"}]},"Based on the search results, here's the information about the Mistral API DELETE /v1/models/{model_id} endpoint:\n\n## DELETE /v1/models/{model_id}\n\nThis endpoint deletes a fine-tuned model.\n\n### Parameters\nThe model_id is a required path parameter (string) that specifies the ID of the model to delete, with an example format like: ft:open-mistral-7b:587a6b29:20240514:7e773925.\n\n### Authentication\nThe endpoint requires ApiKey authentication.\n\n### Response\nThe endpoint returns a 200 status code for a successful response or 422 for validation errors. The response content type is application/json and includes an object with the model id and a \"deleted\": true field.\n\n### Important Restrictions\n